  "findings": [
    "F7 is 0x76. Provider emits a zero-modifier key event only on an allowed subscribed nonbaseline rising edge.",
    "Selected Handler snapshots every matching key and exact modifier callback under its event mutex, then invokes snapshots outside that mutex; one event can invoke multiple consumers.",
    "RegisterKeyBind holds a Lua registry reference and forwards a callback tagged with the mod pointer through Program into Handler. Callback attempts Lua invocation under m_thread_actions_mutex.",
    "The retained mod F7 callback queues toggleMenu through ExecuteInGameThread. Method is the configured default; EngineTick and ProcessEvent use distinct action queues and actual available carriers.",
    "process_simple_actions invokes queued Lua registry functions; toggleMenu calls showMenu. showMenu may return false before changing menuOpen when UI construction fails.",
    "Selected generic Handler returns before provider process_event when is_available is false. The separately retained l22 provider reaches maybe_retry only inside poll; this pair would not drive retries after an unavailable handle. These different snapshots are not a verified built pair."
  ],
  "required_same_run_observations": [
    "Actual deployed runtime, Handler/provider source/build identity and generated map hash; process/run ID and common clock.",
    "Real provider edge ID including raw configured buttons/key/modifiers, allow and subscription, plus enqueue result.",
    "Actual matching registration/consumer identity and callback entry/exit linked to the same edge; record each matched consumer.",
    "Actual ExecuteInGameThread queue method, queued action identity and carrier execution entry/exit linked to that callback.",
    "Actual showMenu success/failure and final visible/menuOpen state. Input enqueue, attempted Lua call or queue insertion alone is insufficient.",
    "Separate hold/release/repress sequence and observed game action behavior for no-repeat/coexistence claims."
